# Gitignored files to copy from the main checkout into a new worktree. One literal path per
# line (file or directory), no globs. Orca reads this file from the main checkout, skips any
# line with `*`, `?` or a leading `!`, and copies a path only if it exists there and is
# gitignored. `claude --worktree` and dotfiles' `wt new` read it in gitignore syntax, where a
# literal path works the same. HANDOFF.md is left out on purpose: each worktree starts its own.
.compound-engineering/config.local.yaml
.claude/settings.local.json
